      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(aws): bootstrap SSH over Tailscale hostname when enabled",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWith `--network tailscale` on the AWS provider, bootstrap readiness probes\nand SSH targets always used the instance public IPv4. When the crabbox\noperator runs on EC2 in the same account/region, AWS drops EC2→EC2\npublic-IP traffic without VPC peering. The leased box joins the tailnet\nvia cloud-init and is reachable there, but `warmup` hangs on the public\nIP probe until timeout.\n\n## Evidence\n\n```console\n$ go test ./internal/providers/aws/ -count=1 -run TestBootstrapSSHHost\nok  github.com/openclaw/crabbox/internal/providers/aws  0.5s\n```\n\n`bootstrapSSHHost` returns the rendered/explicit Tailscale hostname when\nTailscale is enabled, and keeps the public IP when Tailscale is disabled.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** AWS warmup probes public IP under Tailscale, unusable from EC2 operators\n- **Real environment tested:** local `go test` on branch fix/aws-tailscale-bootstrap-probe (no live AWS lease in this session)\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:** `go test ./internal/providers/aws/ -run TestBootstrapSSHHost`\n- **Evidence after fix:** unit proof of host selection; source change on acquire + resolve paths\n- **Observed result after fix:** Tailscale-enabled configs select hostname, disabled keep public IP\n- **What was not tested:** live `crabbox warmup --network tailscale` from an EC2 operator (requires AWS + Tailscale auth)\n\n## Summary\n\n- When `Tailscale.Enabled`, use rendered/explicit Tailscale hostname for bootstrap SSH host\n- Apply on acquire and resolve (instance id + alias)\n- Unit coverage for host selection\n\nCloses #1049\n",
        "branch": "fix/aws-tailscale-bootstrap-probe",
